      {
        "id": "intro-comment",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Normalize a Clip's Audio\n\nEvens out the loudness of a clip recorded too quiet or too loud. It works on video footage because it pulls the audio out first.\n\n**How it works:** The \"Clip\" input goes to \"Extract audio\", which separates the soundtrack. \"Process\" normalizes its level, and \"Audio\" plays the result. It runs locally through ffmpeg with no model or key.\n\n**Try this:** Run it on a quiet phone recording and compare the output level with the original."
        },
